  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preservation of 20th-Century Archival Collections at UMAM Documentation and Research in Beirut</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The archival heritage of Lebanon is crucial for understanding the country&apos;s multifaceted history and promoting civil society. This project aims to conserve and catalog UMAM D&amp;Rs extensive archival collections, making them accessible to the public to enable critical engagement with Lebanon&apos;s past. Activities include organizing and inventorying physical archives, digitizing written and audio-visual materials, launching a digital platform, conducting a social media campaign, hosting online talks, and curating physical exhibitions to enhance public awareness and engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
